<title>Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 8.4.1: Introducing the Zero Product Property </item>
  <item> 8.4.2: Solving Equations of Increasing Complexity Using Reasoning </item>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent">
    <item> 8.4.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 8.4.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 8.4.3: Applying the Zero Product Property to Solve a Real-World Projectile Problem </item>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent">
    <item> 8.4.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 8.4.3: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 8.4.4: Solving Equations Using the Zero Product Property and Reasoning </item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 8.4.5: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Paper and pencil </item>
</list>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> None </item>
</list>
<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. </item>
  <item> Encourage students to look for these words and notice their use and meanings. </item>
  <item> Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in "math talk" and their written and oral explanations. </item>
  <item> Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link>. </item>
</list>
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson:</para>
<table>
  <tgroup cols="2"><thead>
    <row>
      <entry>Previous Vocabulary</entry>
      <entry>New Vocabulary</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <list class="os-raise-noindent">
          <item> quadratic equation </item>
          <item> quadratic function </item>
          <item> factored form (of a quadratic expression) </item>
          <item> standard form (of a quadratic expression) </item>
          <item> variable </item>
          <item> zero of the function </item>
          <item> root </item>
        </list>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <list>
          <item> zero product property </item>
        </list>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</tgroup></table>
